import ../../../testing/driver.dl
import lib/text.dl

appearance small stage appearance:
    maximum width is 100
    height is 30

document painted status:
    paragraph "Status" containing "Waiting" using no UI appearance
    surface "Stage" using small stage appearance

to [finish a test scene while painting] {a pointer to UI canvas frame:painting}:
    set instance to painting's instance
    if (the UI value for (the control labeled "Status" in instance) in instance)'s text = "Waiting":
        set the text of "Status" in instance to "Ready. Your scene is now available."

to [change status before a test frame] {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    set view's frame action to 0 as a pointer
    set the text of "Status" in (view's instance) to "Frame updated"

set instance to an instance of painted status
set window to the address of instance
bind (the control labeled "Stage" in window) in window to (the function named "finish a test scene while painting $") for event 1
set view to a UI view of window sized 120 by 300 using font "regular" with the test UI driver
set next to update UI view (the address of view)
require condition next reporting "A model change during painting did not schedule its next frame."
set status to the UI layout labeled "Status" in (view's layout)
set {waiting height} to status's bounds' height
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition (status's content = "Ready. Your scene is now available.") reporting "A paint callback's model change was acknowledged without rebuilding its paragraph."
require condition (status's bounds' height > waiting height) reporting "A paint callback's longer paragraph retained stale geometry."
set surface to view's window as a pointer to test UI surface
require condition (surface's drawn contains "available.") reporting "The next frame did not draw the updated paragraph."
set paints to surface's paints
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition (surface's paints = paints) reporting "An unchanged model kept repainting after its paint-time update."
set view's frame action to (the function named "change status before a test frame $") as a pointer
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition (status's content = "Frame updated") reporting "A frame callback's model change was acknowledged before layout could consume it."
close the address of view
close window
print line "Paint-time model changes reflow on the next frame, frame callbacks reflow before painting, and unchanged views stay idle."
